Act I: കണക്കിന്റെ പ്രധാന ഘട്ടം.

Scene I: കണക്കിന്റെ ഉപഘട്ടം.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Sebastian and Prospero]
Sebastian: Am I as good as a big hero?
Prospero: If so, let us proceed to scene III.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Duncan and Prospero]
Duncan: Am I as good as nothing?
Prospero: If so, let us proceed to act CIX.
[Exeunt]
[Enter King Lear and Lear]
King Lear: You are as good as King Lear.
[Exeunt]
[Enter King Lear and Prospero]
King Lear: Am I worse than nothing?
Prospero: If so, let us proceed to scene II. Let us proceed to scene III.
[Exeunt]

Scene II: കണക്കിന്റെ ഉപഘട്ടം.
[Exeunt]
[Enter King Lear and Lear]
King Lear: You are as good as the difference between nothing and King Lear. Let us proceed to scene III.
[Exeunt]

Scene III: കണക്കിന്റെ ഉപഘട്ടം.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Caliban and Prospero]
Caliban: You are a hero.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Caliban and Ophelia]
Caliban: You are as good as the difference between a big big big big big big big hero and a hero.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Prospero and Ophelia]

Scene IV: കണക്കിന്റെ ഉപഘട്ടം.
Prospero: Are you better than nothing?
Ophelia:
 If not, let us proceed to scene V.
Prospero: You are as good as the difference between yourself and a hero.
Ophelia:
 You are as good as the product of yourself and a big hero.
 Let us return to scene IV.

Scene V: കണക്കിന്റെ ഉപഘട്ടം.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Caliban and Prospero]
